{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the published documentation URL scheme (JST-287).",
    "Read by scripts/repair-doc-links.py, which writes the `slug:` / `sidebar_position:`",
    "front matter into docs/**.md and expands doc references inside plugins/jira-sdlc/",
    "into published site URLs.",
    "",
    "Slugs are FLAT and DECOUPLED from directory structure on purpose: the sidebar",
    "grouping stays an editorial decision that can be revised without breaking a URL",
    "that already shipped inside someone's plugin cache. See AGENTS.md ->",
    "'The published docs URL scheme'.",
    "",
    "site_docs_base is a contract with JST-288 (website/docusaurus.config.js):",
    "url 'https://kantorv.github.io' + baseUrl '/jira-sdlc-tools/' + docs routeBasePath",
    "'docs'. Changing any of those three breaks every URL baked into the plugin.",
    "",
    "'unpublished' lists files under docs/ that Docusaurus does NOT build, so links to",
    "them from a published doc must be absolute github.com URLs like any other",
    "category-2 link. Docusaurus excludes '_'-prefixed files by default.",
    "",
    "'categories' lists the slugs served by a _category_.json generated-index, i.e.",
    "routes with no backing .md file. They are slugs like any other and must never",
    "change once shipped; they live here so scripts/check-doc-links.sh (category 4)",
    "can validate a link that points at a category index. A published doc must reach",
    "one by ABSOLUTE site URL, not a relative path: the file depth and the slug depth",
    "differ once a page is grouped, so no relative form satisfies both Docusaurus'",
    "URL-relative resolution and the file-relative checker."
  ],
